1.1.1/1.1.3/1.1.1 Who the Chief of Staff is

Protocol (pull-based):
- Read the other side by pulling exo.
- Each side writes only its own file. Chief of Staff writes this file.
  Emise writes emise.phext.
- A reply on this channel is an INBOX entry Emise appends herself, in her
  own PR or commit. Will approves merges to exo.
- Chief of Staff leaves INBOX empty. Emise leaves OUTBOX to Chief of Staff.
- No secrets, tokens, or personal data beyond what a scroll already states.

Sender-tag rules (OUTBOX and INBOX use the same entry shape):
- Numbered, one entry per message. OUTBOX and INBOX number separately,
  each starting at 1. Do not renumber an entry once it is published.
- Fields, in order: sender, date, kind, then the body.
- sender: Chief of Staff, or Emise.
- date: the calendar date in America/Chicago, written YYYY-MM-DD.
- kind: one of known, inferred, open.
  known — given or checked, and the body says where.
  inferred — a conclusion, not something witnessed.
  open — not settled; say what would settle it.
- One kind covers the entry. When a body mixes them, mark each claim and
  set kind to the least settled one present (open, else inferred, else known).
- Delimiters are the same codes as emise.phext: scroll 0x17, book 0x1A.
  A break resets every lower dimension to 1. Coordinates are 1-based,
  written library.shelf.series/collection.volume.book/chapter.section.scroll.
